cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this app, please cite the work it implements (preferred-citation), this release, and Pennsieve (RRID:SCR_021677); the other works it builds on are listed under references.
type: software
title: neuro-encoding
abstract: 'Single-neuron encoding of behaviour: occupancy-normalised tuning curves (pynapple), Skaggs spatial information
  and place fields, speed scores, head-direction tuning, and Poisson GLMs with basis-expanded behaviour covariates
  (NeMoS) with drop-one-covariate deviance, every statistic tested against circular-shift nulls with Benjamini-Hochberg
  FDR. Part of the Pennsieve systems neuroscience workflows.'
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
contact:
- given-names: Joost
  family-names: Wagenaar
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5925-5451
  affiliation: University of Pennsylvania
repository-code: https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/neuro-encoding
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
- neuroscience
- neural-decoding
- electrophysiology
- calcium-imaging
- place-cells
- glm
- tuning-curves
- nwb
# The work this app implements; the release report's "How to cite" puts it first.
